@{
    ViewData["Title"] = ".NET Core Components";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "DotNetCore";
    ViewData["ActivePage"] = "DotNetCoreComponents";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <h1 class="mb-3">Runtime building blocks</h1>
    <p class="lead">Understand the core pieces that ship with .NET Core and how they work together in real deployments.</p>

    <div class="p-4 bg-white border rounded-4 shadow-sm mb-4">
        <h2 class="h5">CLR &amp; Base Class Library</h2>
        <p>The Common Language Runtime (CLR) hosts your managed code, providing JIT compilation, garbage collection, and security boundaries. The Base Class Library (BCL) delivers reusable APIs for collections, networking, file I/O, LINQ, and cryptography.</p>
        <ul class="mb-0">
            <li><strong>Garbage Collector modes:</strong> workstation vs. server GC, plus concurrent options for steady throughput.</li>
            <li><strong>Resource safety:</strong> <code>IDisposable</code> and <code>await using</code> patterns prevent leaks in long-running services.</li>
            <li><strong>Localization:</strong> globalization and resource managers for multi-lingual apps.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="h-100 p-4 bg-white border rounded-4 shadow-sm">
                <h2 class="h5">SDK &amp; CLI</h2>
                <p>The SDK packages compilers, templates, and the <code>dotnet</code> CLI for consistent builds on any OS.</p>
                <ul class="mb-0">
                    <li>Project scaffolding with <code>dotnet new</code> and custom templates.</li>
                    <li>Repeatable builds via <code>dotnet build</code>, <code>dotnet test</code>, and <code>dotnet publish</code>.</li>
                    <li>Extensibility through global tools (<code>dotnet tool install</code>).</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="h-100 p-4 bg-white border rounded-4 shadow-sm">
                <h2 class="h5">Hosting model</h2>
                <p>ASP.NET Core apps run on Kestrel and can be reverse-proxied by Nginx, Apache, IIS, or cloud load balancers.</p>
                <ul class="mb-0">
                    <li><strong>Generic Host:</strong> unifies configuration, logging, and dependency injection for web and worker services.</li>
                    <li><strong>Configuration pipeline:</strong> layered providers (JSON, env vars, Key Vault, user secrets) with strong binding.</li>
                    <li><strong>Health checks &amp; metrics:</strong> endpoints ready for probes in AKS, Kubernetes, and App Service.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
